{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"1f743d96afc8439bb1336f800c4d85fec6cf79713730be766d55b7415d653507","packTokens":2283,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"side","tokens":100,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":79,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":880,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1119,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PRODUCT SIDE. This run builds the API side of the product these requirements describe, in an existing .NET API project: every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there, and the data behind them. The web app is built in its own repo: no screen is built here, and no criterion is written for one.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build the API side in the existing .NET API project.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation in contracts/openapi.yaml exactly as written.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement the data behind the API operations.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the backend persist and execute the broader product workflows only when an operation in the locked OpenAPI contract exposes them, or should it also build data/workflows for capabilities that the contract does not expose?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement the data and business rules needed by contracted operations only; do not add uncontracted API operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For contracted operations, should access enforcement include the detailed warehouse, organisation, and role restrictions described in the user stories, beyond whatever security is declared in the OpenAPI contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce the user stories' explicit restrictions on contracted data: customer-organisation isolation, warehouse assignments, staff roles, and Auditor read-only access, without changing the API surface.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Where the contracted receipt operations expose stock receipt behavior, which of the narrative receipt and quality rules must the API enforce and persist?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the explicit receipt rules where exposed: separate traceable receipt records even for repeated product/lot pairs, quarantine on receipt, Quality Officer release, and the stated expiry restrictions.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For contracted customer-order and allocation operations, how much of the described order lifecycle should be implemented beyond basic persistence of contract fields?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the explicit order rules where exposed: customer changes/cancellation only before packing, duplicate-submission protection, suitable-stock allocation, and the stated allocation and back-order behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How broad should the audit history be for contracted data changes? The request requires an audit trail and says records can be changed after the fact, but does not define the complete event set or immutability behavior.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Store actor and time for consequential changes and decisions exposed by contracted operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must audit events for consequential changes and decisions remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain audit events without automatic expiry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to the existing spreadsheet-based operational data when the API is introduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not migrate legacy data; start with records entered through the contracted API operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When the configured database is unavailable or invalid, what should the API do beyond the existing fail-fast behavior for a missing connection string?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup for invalid configuration and return the contract-defined server error for failed operations; never report a business operation as successful.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation, schema, parameter, header, media type, and status in the locked OpenAPI contract under `/api` in the existing ASP.NET Core .NET 9 project, without adding uncontracted business operations, while preserving the root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist the contracted records, relationships, state changes, files, and audit events in the configured shared database; retain successful changes across restarts, exclude legacy business data, support deployment bootstrap and opt-in demo seeding, and fail startup or return the contracted server error when storage is unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the contracted staff authorization-URL lookup and customer sign-in, one-time-code verification and resend, and password-reset flows with email delivery, configured attempt limits, and the contract-defined responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Authenticate staff through the configured Meridian Microsoft identity provider, map them to active persisted accounts, keep staff authentication separate from customer authentication, and enforce organisation, role, warehouse, Auditor read-only, and account-status access restrictions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement searchable products and immutable, versioned temperature profiles with required profiles, validated tiers, governance history, and deactivation behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement receipt, receipt-logger, receipt-evidence, stock, movement, and opening-stock records and workflows, including quarantine, traceability, expiry validation, Quality Officer release, and their separate two-person approval rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Run expiry checks using each warehouse’s configured local time zone, mark expired handling units, remove or replace allocations under the contracted rules, update order status, record changes, and alert dispatchers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer orders and dispatch allocations using configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and shelf-life rules, enforcing idempotency, order validation, customer changes, cancellation, stock eligibility, allocation priority, back orders, and overrides.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualifications, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, delivery evidence, and driver-change notifications.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Process receipt-upload and authenticated gateway logger readings, support concurrent logger and cold-room readings, and expose contracted temperature histories, gaps, excursions, tier budgets, holds, alerts, and corrected history for late or out-of-order readings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records; enforce two-person approval where required, apply the latest valid disposition to extant stock, and retain prior decision history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Implement signed recalls, lot tracing, affected-stock allocation blocks, customer recall responses, and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations, scoped to the authenticated organisation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organisation shelf-life settings, account roles and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Record actor and timestamp for consequential changes and decisions in read-only audit events, support contracted filtering, and retain events without automatic expiry.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}